DESCRIPTION >
    Daily OHLCV bars, RAW (not split-adjusted), in the instrument's quote currency.
    Decimals follow Merton ADR-NUM-04 (8 places, 15 integer digits) and arrive as decimal strings.
    close is the value Merton imports as instrument_prices.price for price_date (ADR-VAL-06).
    Primary source: EODHD /api/eod/{SYMBOL} (OHLC are raw).
    Fallback: Yahoo chart API, whose OHLC are split-adjusted; the ingester converts them back to raw
    with the splits dated after each bar and rounds to Yahoo's priceHint.
    volume is split-adjusted, as both EODHD and Yahoo deliver it.
    adjusted_close is the source's split+dividend adjusted close AT FETCH TIME and goes stale after each
    new split or dividend; derive adjusted series from dividends + stock_splits instead.
    Highest version wins per (symbol, price_date); query with FINAL.
    Same key from both sources: EODHD always wins over Yahoo; within a source the latest fetch wins
    (version = source rank x 10^13 + ingest epoch ms; EODHD rank 2, YAHOO rank 1).

SCHEMA >
    `symbol` String `json:$.symbol`,
    `price_date` Date32 `json:$.price_date`,
    `open` Decimal(23, 8) `json:$.open`,
    `high` Decimal(23, 8) `json:$.high`,
    `low` Decimal(23, 8) `json:$.low`,
    `close` Decimal(23, 8) `json:$.close`,
    `adjusted_close` Decimal(23, 8) `json:$.adjusted_close`,
    `volume` UInt64 `json:$.volume`,
    `source` LowCardinality(String) `json:$.source`,
    `ingested_at` DateTime64(3) `json:$.ingested_at`,
    `version` UInt64 `json:$.version`

ENGINE "ReplacingMergeTree"
ENGINE_VER version
ENGINE_SORTING_KEY "symbol, price_date"
ENGINE_PARTITION_KEY "toYear(price_date)"

TOKEN ingest_token APPEND
